    <!-- Resume_Link_Base_URL__c IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS FILE.
         Not blank; absent. The two are very different here, and the
         difference used to make this record's own instruction impossible to
         follow.

         A site URL is org state, not source: it differs per org and
         scripts/check-references.py rightly flags a committed one. So it is set
         directly in the target org (docs/runbooks/questionnaire-resume.md).
         But this file previously carried an explicit <value xsi:nil="true"/>
         for it, and a custom-metadata deploy WRITES the fields it lists, so
         every ./scripts/deploy.sh silently re-blanked the value an operator had
         just been told to set, and resume emails stopped going out with no
         error anywhere.

         Verified against gtm-dev before making this change: deploying this
         record with the field OMITTED leaves the org's existing value intact,
         which is exactly the behaviour wanted. Do not "tidy" the field back in
         with a nil value.

         Until it is set in a given org, GtmAssessmentDraftController falls back
         to Site.getBaseSecureUrl() and, failing that, declines to send a resume
         email rather than sending one with a broken or foreign link in it. -->
</CustomMetadata>
